---
id: PY-006
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'print() in production code'
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 1

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '(^|[^.\w])print\s*\('

related: [PY-004]
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

A shipped `print()` is unstructured output with no level, timestamp, or sink
control; in a service it pollutes stdout and is invisible to the log pipeline.
Use the `logging` module instead: `logging.getLogger(__name__).debug(...)`.
This rule is opt-in — enable it for services and libraries where stdout is not
the product. (A CLI that legitimately prints to stdout should leave it off.)
